 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Wheat for the deeds never lost, footsteps for the emigrants, a house for those driven from their homes. Nothing for the fighting or for Paradise (195:30-43, no river). STAGING v4: 195: a group of believing men and women (a people group, a woman among them, for «من ذكر أو أنثى») on the road; on «هاجروا» they walk on (emigration), the house plate for the homes they were driven from, bow on «وأوذوا». The fighting and the killed (195:25-26) are not drawn and nobody leaves the stage. Paradise and its rivers are never drawn: only a light plate from «جنات», and the people raise their hands on «حسن الثواب»."
 },
